  "description": "The 162 Poor Law Unions of Ireland after Newport Union was dissolved into Westport on 30 Sep 1885, until Donaghmore was dissolved on 30 Sep 1886. Derived from the 5 Apr 1891 map with Gortin and Donaghmore given back the divisions they held in 1851. Divisions that moved between unions at dates not established between 1851 and 1891 are drawn as in 1891; most of those moves were of parts of divisions (Knockatooan, Tullaghmelan, Burtonhall, the Clare part of Gort, Holycross, Longfordpass, Cloonbur, Kilmovee, Ballymoe, Cullenwaine), which the 1907-12 division map cannot show. See Poor Law Unions 5 Apr 1891 for the method and the checks against the printed areas, which apply here. The map is simplified for display by a coverage simplification of the division map, so neighbouring unions keep common edges (95% of divisions lie within 10 m of the full lines); the full-resolution file is among the downloads.",
